  "final_assessment": "15 of 18 tasks done. The engine now computes severity-aware convergence, the blind pair, and the budget reported beside the state. Two conventions are implemented ONCE rather than per rule: freshness lives only at the evaluateReviewed call site, and every rule states its empty case. Clause (b) is existence-first then one readability predicate with one fallback, reading the disposition from `outcome` or legacy `status`. Clause (c) is the SHIPPED predicate with one edit — the new-finding match is substantive — since the pass-set redesign left for rc02c. Clause (a) is an existential search WITH BACKTRACKING; the blind-pair slot takes two passes of distinct independent classes, both later than the previous slot's passes AND its resolution records, blind with endpoints inclusive, ties rejected. The budget carries two counts: `independentSpend` (whole trail, stale and rejected returns included, display only) and `independentSpendFresh` (the trigger), with `budgetExhausted` and the BUDGET-SPENT position tokens keyed off the trigger. All four fields reach BOTH gate-row projections. `commandForClass` is exhaustive over CadenceEntry and the blind-pair recommendation tests PAIRABILITY rather than existence. Cadence-entry validation moved off the Zod enum so the error names the gate id rather than an array index — the exact defect the fourth review predicted, reproduced by a test on the first run. Schema is v4. Suite 2041 to 2086 (45 new rc02 cases, every rule walked on a hand-written trail); seven pre-existing tests updated for the bump: three schema-version assertions, three report goldens whose engine tail legitimately changed, one loader fixture reshaped to the v4 cadence, plus two re-pinned template hashes. Sweep closed five stale post-apply next-command sites: the three verify-emit branches now read the gate graph through one helper rather than hardcoding `--as system`, and two body predictions were reworded.",
